                            profile[\\\"deferred_free_ms\\\"] = (\\ntiered_serve/chunk_delta3_kv_compressor.py:2359:                - (profile[\\\"deferred_free_ms\\\"] or 0.0))\\ncpp_extensions/csrc/kv_slot_allocator.cpp:21:class KVSlotAllocator {\\n\"}"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"i\":2,\"output\":\"# CSR garbage policies\\n\\nThese experiments use the original CD3 CSR storage and decoder. Dedicated KV\\ncapacity, GPU staging capacity, and attention kernels are unchanged. The\\nstarting point is remote `origin/main` at\\n`19a15c5d66d14481acb7e00c5e6f371d8ffb0964`.\\n\\nBoth performance suites accept `--cd3-kv-csr-policy append|compact|reuse`.\\nSpecify the policy explicitly when comparing experiments; policies require\\n`--cd3-kv-storage csr`.\\nStandalone callers set `TIERED_SERVE_KV_CD3_CSR_POLICY`.\\n\\nThe subsequent [CPU optimization](cd3-cpu-path.md) is selectable with\\n`--cd3-kv-cpu-path legacy|optimized` (default: `optimized`). The original\\npolicy-only measurements in [the earlier report](cd3-csr-results.md) used\\nthe legacy CPU path; [the CPU report](cd3-cpu-results.md) separates stages.\\n\\n| Policy | Retirement | New encoded entries |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `append` | Mark old words as garbage | Append; retain existing capacity-pressure rebuilds |\\n| `compact` | Repack the remaining live entries after each physical retirement batch | Repack if overwriting records creates garbage; otherwise append |\\n| `reuse` | Coalesce freed ranges and trim a free tail | Best-fit hole first, then append; rebuild on capacity/fragmentation failure |\\n\\nThe `compact` policy publishes new pinned entries and offsets. Older plans keep\\ntheir original tensors until H2D completes. It preserves allocated capacity\\nbut reduces `used_words`, which controls contiguous entries transfers. Returning\\nmemory to the OS is not required to remove garbage from H2D.\\n\\nThe `reuse` policy uses indices ordered by address and by `(size, address)`.\\nAdjacent free ranges merge. A remainder smaller than eight 64-bit words stays\\nwith its allocation, allowing at most 56 bytes of internal slack per such\\nallocation. Logical entry counts remain exact. The free tail is removed from\\n`used_words` immediately. The optimized serial path can omit up to three large\\nholes per K/V arena, using at most four entries descriptors per side in the\\nexisting batch-copy call. Smaller holes and internal slack remain in the copy.\\nOffsets do not change: a range at host offset X is copied to GPU offset X.\\nStaging still reserves the full address extent, and capacity repack remains\\nunchanged. Repacked plans do not use the original allocator's hole snapshot.\\n\\nThe immutable snapshot comes from the allocator's size index only when a new\\nplan is built. Cached submissions do not search holes, walk live records or\\nallocate new descriptors. Payload writes still wait for the preceding H2D,\\nincluding writes to small holes that remain inside copied ranges.\\n\\nThe fixed omission threshold is **133592 bytes**. A one-time GH200 calibration\\nof the same `CSRSerialKVPlan.submit` batch backend estimated 333329 bytes/us and\\n0.400766 us per extra descriptor, including two standard errors of the fit.\\nThe threshold rounds their product up to an eight-byte word. A hole is omitted\\nonly when its size exceeds that threshold; request rate does not tune it.\\n`scripts/calibrate_cd3_csr_copy.py --output calibration.json` reproduces the\\nmeasurement on an idle GPU. It is a copy cost model, not proof of model speed.\\n\\nFor every CSR policy, optimized serial submission now registers staging reuse\\nwait, H2D, source completion, decode dependency, the existing paired decoder,\\nand staging consumption in one native call. Python accounting follows GPU\\nsubmission. The two fixed streams, two staging rings and dense-reader gates\\nretain their existing roles; there is no additional kernel or resident KV.\\n\\nRetirement only changes allocation metadata in `reuse` mode. The existing\\nencoder waits for the layer's preceding H2D before overwriting any body or\\nentries bytes. If an encoder is pending, physical retirement remains deferred\\nuntil that writer stops. This applies to both new policies.\\n\\nBest-fit retirement validates the common K/V slot batch once and returns both\\nallocator layouts in one native call. Each allocator coalesces newly freed\\nadjacent ranges before changing its hole indices, so a contiguous batch does\\nnot repeatedly erase and recreate a growing hole. Scratch vectors retain their\\ncapacity. The same range batching handles overwritten records during reserve.\\nThese changes retain the synchronous callback and its ownership rules; they\\nreduce its bookkeeping rather than moving retirement to another thread.\\n\\n## Measurement\\n\\n`cd3_csr_garbage_bytes` counts dead entries and internal slack actually included\\nin CD3 H2D submissions. It is a subset of `cd3_gap_bytes`: the latter also\\nincludes entries of live but inactive blocks. If the existing capacity fallback\\npacks selected entries, its transferred garbage is zero. A policy does not\\nclaim to remove live-but-inactive data.\\n`cd3_csr_skipped_bytes` counts holes omitted from actual submissions. Repeated\\nchunks count their own avoided transfers; this is not allocator free capacity.\\n\\nThe serving suite's `--kv-byte-metrics` records per-forward byte counters\\nwithout enabling GPU timing. All compared policies must use the same option.\\nByte totals cover all server forwards, whereas the client's request trimming\\nonly affects client latency statistics.\\n\\nAt worker shutdown, `CD3 CSR totals` logs compaction count, bytes repacked,\\nbytes placed in holes, bytes appended, and bytes retired. Its\\n`sum_peak_used_bytes` is the sum of individual layer/side high-water marks,\\nnot a simultaneously measured process-memory peak.\\n\\nThe bounded comparison uses real requests from the existing Azure trace:\\n\\n```bash\\nfor policy in append compact reuse; do\\n  bash scripts/serving/run_performance_suite.sh \\\\\\n    --codecs cd3 --modes kvcomp \\\\\\n    --cd3-kv-storage csr --cd3-kv-csr-policy \\\"$policy\\\" \\\\\\n    --cd3-kv-execution serial \\\\\\n    --chunks 8192 --request-rates 4 --max-num-seqs 64 \\\\\\n    --dedicated-kv-blocks 2432 \\\\\\n    --num-prompts 192 --skip-first-n-requests 16 \\\\\\n    --skip-last-n-requests 16 --repeats 1 --kv-byte-metrics \\\\\\n    --output-root \\\"benchmark_results/cd3_csr/$policy\\\"\\ndone\\n```\\n\\nCompaction removes all dead entries but copies the live entries repeatedly.\\nReuse avoids most movement but can retain scattered holes. A possible follow-up\\nis reuse with occasional compaction when measured wasted transfers justify the\\ncopy cost. A fixed threshold is a heuristic, not an optimality guarantee;\\nthe two policies above isolate the tradeoff before adding that combination.\\n        else\\n            v.encode_block(task / 2);\\n    }\\n}\\n\\n// Append planning uses private reusable CPU buffers, never H2D-visible storage.\\nusing HostWordCounts = py::array_t<int64_t, py::array::c_style>;\\n\\nvoid check_host_long_vector(const torch::Tensor& tensor, const char* name)\\n{\\n    TORCH_CHECK(tensor.device().is_cpu() && tensor.is_contiguous()\\n                    && tensor.dim() == 1 && tensor.scalar_type() == at::kLong,\\n                name, \\\" must be a contiguous CPU int64 vector\\\");\\n}\\n\\n#include \\\"chunk_delta3_csr_free_list.h\\\"\\n#include \\\"chunk_delta3_csr_compact.h\\\"\\n\\nstd::pair<int64_t, int64_t> prepare_host_chunk_delta3_csr_append(\\n    torch::Tensor num_exceptions,\\n    torch::Tensor slots,\\n    const HostWordCounts& previous_word_counts,\\n    torch::Tensor word_counts,\\n    torch::Tensor relative_offsets,\\n    int64_t packed_capacity)\\n{\\n    TORCH_CHECK(num_exceptions.device().is_cpu()\\n                    && num_exceptions.dim() == 1\\n                    && num_exceptions.scalar_type() == at::kInt\\n                    && num_exceptions.stride(0) >= 1,\\n                \\\"num_exceptions must be a CPU int32 vector\\\");\\n    check_host_long_vector(slots, \\\"slots\\\");\\n    check_host_long_vector(word_counts, \\\"word_counts\\\");\\n    check_host_long_vector(relative_offsets, \\\"relative_offsets\\\");\\n    TORCH_CHECK(word_counts.numel() == slots.numel()\\n                    && relative_offsets.numel() == slots.numel(),\\n                \\\"CSR append scratch must match slots\\\");\\n    TORCH_CHECK(previous_word_counts.ndim() == 1\\n                    && previous_word_counts.size() == num_exceptions.numel(),\\n                \\\"previous word counts must match source slots\\\");\\n    TORCH_CHECK(packed_capacity > 0\\n                    && packed_capacity <= std::numeric_limits<int64_t>::max() / 3,\\n                \\\"invalid packed entry capacity\\\");\\n    const int64_t* ids = slots.data_ptr<int64_t>();\\n    const int32_t* counts = num_exceptions.data_ptr<int32_t>();\\n    const int64_t* previous = previous_word_counts.data();\\n    int64_t* words = word_counts.data_ptr<int64_t>();\\n    int64_t* offsets = relative_offsets.data_ptr<int64_t>();\\n    int64_t append_words = 0;\\n    int64_t old_words = 0;\\n    for (int64_t row = 0; row < slots.numel(); ++row) {\\n        const int64_t slot = ids[row];\\n        TORCH_CHECK(slot >= 0 && slot < num_exceptions.numel(),\\n                    \\\"CSR append slot out of range: \\\", slot);\\n        const int64_t count = counts[slot * num_exceptions.stride(0)];\\n        TORCH_CHECK(count >= 0 && previous[slot] >= 0,\\n                    \\\"negative CSR exception or previous word count\\\");\\n        const int64_t stored = std::min(count, packed_capacity * 3);\\n        const int64_t row_words = (stored + 2) / 3;\\n        TORCH_CHECK(row_words <= std::numeric_limits<int64_t>::max() - append_words\\n                        && previous[slot] <= std::numeric_limits<int64_t>::max() - old_words,\\n                    \\\"CSR append word sum overflow\\\");\\n        words[row] = row_words;\\n        offsets[row] = append_words;\\n        append_words += row_words;\\n        old_words += previous[slot];\\n    }\\n    return {append_words, old_words};\\n}\\n\\nvoid append_host_chunk_delta3_csr(\\n    torch::Tensor entries20x3,\\n    torch::Tensor slots,\\n    torch::Tensor word_counts,\\n    torch::Tensor relative_offsets,\\n    torch::Tensor destination_entries,\\n    torch::Tensor destination_offsets,\\n    HostWordCounts destination_word_counts,\\n    int64_t base,\\n    int64_t append_words)\\n{\\n    TORCH_CHECK(entries20x3.device().is_cpu()\\n                    && entries20x3.dim() == 2\\n                    && entries20x3.scalar_type() == at::kLong\\n                    && entries20x3.stride(1) == 1\\n                    && entries20x3.stride(0) >= entries20x3.size(1),\\n                \\\"entries20x3 must be a row-major CPU int64 matrix\\\");\\n    check_host_long_vector(slots, \\\"slots\\\");\\n    check_host_long_vector(word_counts, \\\"word_counts\\\");\\n    check_host_long_vector(relative_offsets, \\\"relative_offsets\\\");\\n    check_host_long_vector(destination_entries, \\\"destination_entries\\\");\\n    check_host_long_vector(destination_offsets, \\\"destination_offsets\\\");\\n    TORCH_CHECK(word_counts.numel() == slots.numel()\\n                    && relative_offsets.numel() == slots.numel(),\\n                \\\"CSR append plan must match slots\\\");\\n    TORCH_CHECK(destination_word_counts.ndim() == 1\\n                    && destination_word_counts.writeable()\\n                    && destination_word_counts.size() == entries20x3.size(0)\\n                    && destination_offsets.numel() == entries20x3.size(0),\\n                \\\"CSR destination metadata must match source slots and be writable\\\");\\n    TORCH_CHECK(base >= 0 && base <= destination_entries.numel()\\n                    && append_words >= 0\\n                    && append_words <= destination_entries.numel() - base,\\n                \\\"CSR append exceeds destination capacity\\\");\\n    const int64_t* ids = slots.data_ptr<int64_t>();\\n    const int64_t* words = word_counts.data_ptr<int64_t>();\\n    const int64_t* offsets = relative_offsets.data_ptr<int64_t>();\\n    int64_t total = 0;\\n    // Validate the complete plan before writing payload or publishing metadata.\\n    // The plan owns the count calculation; no exception counts are reread here.\\n    for (int64_t row = 0; row < slots.numel(); ++row) {\\n        TORCH_CHECK(ids[row] >= 0 && ids[row] < entries20x3.size(0),\\n                    \\\"CSR append slot out of range: \\\", ids[row]);\\n        TORCH_CHECK(words[row] >= 0 && words[row] <= entries20x3.size(1)\\n                        && words[row] <= append_words - total\\n                        && offsets[row] == total,\\n                    \\\"invalid CSR append prefix or word count\\\");\\n        total += words[row];\\n    }\\n    TORCH_CHECK(total == append_words, \\\"CSR append plan size mismatch\\\");\\n    const int64_t* source = entries20x3.data_ptr<int64_t>();\\n    int64_t* destination = destination_entries.data_ptr<int64_t>();\\n    int64_t* published_offsets = destination_offsets.data_ptr<int64_t>();\\n    int64_t* published_words = destination_word_counts.mutable_data();\\n    const int64_t stride = entries20x3.stride(0);\\n    const int64_t rows = slots.numel();\\n    py::gil_scoped_release no_gil;\\n#pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) if(rows >= 64)\\n    for (int64_t row = 0; row < rows; ++row) {\\n        if (words[row] != 0) {\\n            std::memcpy(destination + base + offsets[row],\\n                        source + ids[row] * stride,\\n                        static_cast<size_t>(words[row]) * sizeof(int64_t));\\n        }\\n    }\\n    for (int64_t row = 0; row < rows; ++row) {\\n        published_offsets[ids[row]] = base + offsets[row];\\n        published_words[ids[row]] = words[row];\\n    }\\n}\\n\\nvoid pack_host_chunk_delta3_entries_csr(\\n    torch::Tensor entries20x3,\\n    torch::Tensor num_exceptions,\\n    torch::Tensor storage_slots,\\n    torch::Tensor packed_output,\\n    torch::Tensor entry_word_offsets)\\n{\\n    TORCH_CHECK(!entries20x3.is_cuda()\\n                    && entries20x3.scalar_type() == at::kLong\\n                    && entries20x3.dim() == 2\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0d353-8a6b-74f3-a788-77c13b90cdc3","create_time":1790251901.3600256}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
